      "review": "Whole calm right-facing Collector with closed interlocking chest, finger-crown, long doubled forearms, slatted shoulder/hip plates, seal, divided heavy mantle, wrapped shins, feet and held crescent staff. Native imagegen correction lifts only lowest cape ends to sole/staff baseline; no floor or second figure. Both complete external contour and actual RGBA transparency verified.",
      "limits": "One newly authored static side presentation; no canonical animation, opposite-side anatomy, exact staff ornament geometry, source timing or fidelity1:1 certification. Source colors in the episode are amber-lit; artist says sculpt textures unfinished. Corpus portal behavior is retained unchanged; this image depicts closed resting torso seen in final scene. Margins are smaller than the prompt asks (staff near y50) but all solid tips remain in frame. Tiny alpha1 fringe exists around the opaque silhouette; see exact alpha8/32 bounds. Further runtime visual QA is required before acceptance."
