      "review": "One collective image contains exactly three distinct complete right-facing insect profiles. Three separated alpha32 column groups corroborate the visual count. Each has a low segmented carapace, tapered rear tail, jointed legs and small human-like face integrated beneath the anterior shell; no separate human body is invented. The outer legs and all tails remain within the image. A few far legs are naturally occluded by near legs. The three support lines differ by only three native pixels. The result retains the earlier prototype count of three while explicitly treating it as a representative sample, not a canonical swarm size.",
      "limits": "The source mesh is a production side-view sample and the construction prop predates final facial detailing; the final-film ventral close-up controls that detail. Generated surfaces, the opposite side, leg offsets and face projection remain reconstructions. The prompt requested 8 percent border; the nearest readable alpha8 silhouette is 28 pixels from the left edge (1.29 percent of native width), so the requested horizontal margin is not met, although no readable appendage is cut. Low-alpha native noise touches canvas edges and is preserved. The sprite is wide because all three complete insects share one support line. The proposed bodyHeight is a standing-equivalent presentation calibration to keep the collective footprint usable, not a measured source height. One actor profile, one static idle, no independent swarm actors, no source motion/cadence claim and no 1:1 certification. Root must inspect gameplay placement and scale.",
      "singleCollectiveProfileReviewed": true,
      "priorDisplayedSubjectCount": 3,
      "priorFrameSHA256": "8171253b7eed7045da6e7e09ab2059c314b34e0506e3fd0713160458951a6b57"
    },
